  message: "Pass-34 batch (3 findings — `--frameworks` flag effect on substrate, exercising probe class queued by pass 33).\n\n**F34.A1 — Validator scope-incomplete: `--frameworks all` produces 33 validation violations vs 0 in default mode.** Generated 3 fresh substrates (default auto-detect, --frameworks all, --frameworks none) on hypergumbo's own codebase. Violations breakdown (`/tmp/p34_fw_all.json:.validation_report.violations`):\n- 19× axis_conformance on Symbol.origin = 'route-materializer' (not in the pass-id catalog of 179 known values)\n- 1× axis_conformance on AnalysisRun.pass_id = 'view-template-linker' (not in catalog)\n- 11× id_format on Symbol.id from grpc-linker — format `grpc:/path:LINE:NAME:KIND` where span is single integer line (e.g., `:1170:`) instead of canonical `start-end` form (`:1170-1170:`)\n- 2× id_format on Symbol.stable_id = 'CreateUser' / 'GetUsers' — graphql-linker emits literal operation names, not sha256: form\n\nThe INV-sugat closure satisfaction claim of \"zero violations across all five validator classes on self-analysis\" holds for the default-auto-detect substrate only. Framework linkers (django-third-party-dispatch, view-template, grpc, graphql) are gated out of self-analysis because they don't fire on hypergumbo's own codebase — hypergumbo doesn't expose Django models, GraphQL schemas, or gRPC services. When `--frameworks all` forcibly activates them, 3 of 5 validator classes light up immediately:\n- axis_conformance (20 of 33)\n- id_format (13 of 33)\n- writer_contract / cross_field / verdict_enum (0 of 33 — these classes hold)\n\nThe WI-kafar CI gate (test_validation_report_empty.py) locks in zero-violation state — but only against the substrate the test fixture generates, which is the default-auto-detect path. The gate has a coverage blind spot for framework-linker code paths.\n\n**F34.A2 — Feature emission gated on auto-detect mode only.** Both `--frameworks all` AND `--frameworks none` produce ZERO features (vs default's 16). The `all` value is intuitively a superset of auto-detect; in practice it's `[]`. The flag value `none` and `all` BOTH disable feature emission entirely, while leaving entrypoint emission (104 → 104/105), UC emission (8 → 8), and basic node/edge counts intact. Feature emission is a third, distinct gate beyond `entrypoint` detection and `meta.framework_role` tagging. Per pass-33 F33.18, all 16 features in default substrate come from `hypergumbo-tracker/serve.py` (auto-detected as starlette); pass-34 quantifies the gate at the flag level.\n\n**F34.A3 — `--frameworks all` profile.frameworks = 171 entries (full catalog dump).** profile.frameworks lists the flag value verbatim — all 171 frameworks the catalog knows — regardless of detection. 11 distinct framework_role values appear in actual node.meta data (websocket_endpoint, event_subscriber, event_publisher, grpc_servicer, grpc_stub, http_client, graphql_resolver, route, mq_publisher, mq_subscriber, graphql_client). **Intersection between the 171 declared frameworks and the 11 observed framework_role values: 0.** The two surfaces use disjoint vocabularies: profile.frameworks lists framework-package names (django, flask, starlette, lit, react, vue, ...); meta.framework_role uses role-pattern names (route, http_client, event_publisher, ...). Same finding-family as pass-25 F25.17 (profile.frameworks=['lit','starlette'] with 0 node-level references) — pass-34 extends to scale with `--frameworks all` (83× more declared frameworks).\n\n**Concrete fix-path candidates:**\n1. Extend `test_validation_report_empty.py` (WI-kafar) to a 3-substrate matrix: default + `--frameworks all` + `--frameworks none`. The default-substrate gate doesn't catch F34.A1's 33 violations.\n2. Wire framework-linker writers (django-third-party-dispatch, grpc, graphql, view-template, route-materializer) through the canonical Symbol.id factory + `make_typed_stable_id` to fix the 13 id_format violations.\n3. Register `route-materializer` and `view-template-linker` in the pass-id catalog (or rename to existing catalog entries) to fix the 20 axis_conformance violations.\n4. Either: (a) document that `--frameworks all`/`none` disables feature emission, (b) wire feature detection to fire regardless of flag value, or (c) make the flag's effect explicit in --help.\n5. Either: (a) filter profile.frameworks to detected-only at emission time, (b) document the field as \"flag value echoed verbatim\", or (c) split into profile.frameworks_requested vs profile.frameworks_detected.\n\n**Why on INV-luhur.** All three findings sit at the meta-layer writer-contract scope this META umbrellas. F34.A1 is sub-pattern 1 (writer-wired-without-validator-cross-check applied to framework-linker writers); F34.A2 is a mode-conditional writer (sub-pattern 2 extended to flag-conditional emission); F34.A3 is sub-pattern 1 at the profile.frameworks field (writer echoes input without validation against actual emission).\n\n**Probe artifacts:** `/tmp/p34_fw_all.json` (140.8 MB) + `/tmp/p34_fw_none.json` (140.6 MB) substrates; `/tmp/p34_outputA.log` (basic delta) + `/tmp/p34_outputA2.log` (violation breakdown, ARs, framework_role distribution); `/tmp/p34_probeA.py` / `/tmp/p34_probeA2.py` probe scripts. No status change."  # 80da
- op: discuss  # 6914
