  nonce: '6914'  # 6914
  message: "Pass-35 batch (2 findings — second validator-scope blind spot, profile.frameworks 3-mode semantics).\n\n**F35.A1 — `--include-docs` produces 4321 validation violations vs default 0.** Pass-34 F34.A1 found 33 violations on `--frameworks all` (framework-linker writers). Pass-35 finds the SECOND blind spot at 130× scale: doc/config analyzers (markdown + gitignore) gated behind `--include-docs` ALSO escape the validator's self-analysis CI gate (WI-kafar test fixture uses default flags).\n\nAll 4321 violations are `id_format` class. Field breakdown:\n- 827× Symbol.id from markdown analyzer (sections/code_blocks/links with kinds section/code_block/link)\n- 3494× Symbol.stable_id (gitignore patterns + markdown sections)\n\nOrigins: markdown=4243, gitignore=78. Distinct message families: 176. Three sub-mechanisms dominate (filed separately on INV-kurup for the id-construction face):\n1. gitignore writers REUSE Symbol.id as Symbol.stable_id (2667 cases — `composite_no_sha_prefix colon_count=4`)\n2. markdown section IDs include section-title literal colons (825 cases — `composite_no_sha_prefix colon_count=5`)\n3. markdown code_block uses 'code' as span segment (584 cases — `malformed_span_segment`)\n\n**Two blind spots so far** (cumulative pass-34 + pass-35 finding pattern):\n- Framework linkers (gated by `--frameworks all`): 33 violations\n- Doc/config analyzers (gated by `--include-docs`): 4321 violations\n\nIn both cases the underlying writers were NEVER migrated to the canonical factories the INV-sugat closure campaign mandated. The closure's \"zero violations\" claim and WI-kafar CI gate operate against the default substrate fixture. Neither blind-spot category fires during default self-analysis.\n\nFull sweep of 6 substrate modes (default, --fw all, --fw none, --first-party-only, --include-docs, --max-tier 4) confirms violations fire ONLY on the two modes that activate writers NOT exercised by default self-analysis. The 4 other modes produce 0 violations. This is a structural pattern: validator scope = default-substrate scope.\n\n**F35.A3 — profile.frameworks has 3 distinct semantics across flag modes.** Sweep across 6 modes:\n- DEFAULT, FIRST_PARTY, INCLUDE_DOCS, MAX_TIER_4: ['lit', 'starlette'] (detection-derived per substrate content)\n- FW_ALL: 171 entries (full catalog dump, per pass-34 F34.A3)\n- FW_NONE: [] (silenced entirely)\n\nSame field — 3 distinct behaviors. Pass-34 F34.A3 documented the catalog-dump face; pass-35 confirms detection is consistent across 4 other modes AND adds the `--fw none` silenced-entirely face. Cross-mode survey establishes that the field carries 3 semantic categories with no in-record signal to distinguish them — consumers reading profile.frameworks cannot tell which mode produced the value without out-of-band knowledge.\n\n**Concrete fix-path candidates** (cumulative across pass-34 + pass-35):\n1. Extend WI-kafar CI gate to a 6-substrate matrix (default + 5 flag modes). Default-only fixture has missed 4354 violations across 2 modes.\n2. Migrate markdown analyzer and gitignore analyzer to `make_symbol_id` + `make_*_stable_id` factories. 3494 violations have the gitignore-stable_id mechanism alone; that one targeted change closes ~80% of F35.A1.\n3. Document or split profile.frameworks. Three options: split into `frameworks_requested` vs `frameworks_detected`; deprecate the flag-echo behavior and always emit detected; document the 3-mode semantics.\n\n**Probe artifacts:** `/tmp/p35_docs.json` (142 MB substrate); `/tmp/p35_probeA.py` validator-scope sweep script; `/tmp/p35_outputA.log` (violation breakdown across 6 modes). No status change."  # 6914
- op: discuss  # 334d
