  clock: 15  # 334d
  nonce: 334d  # 334d
  message: "Pass 36 (continuing 06022026_1622) batch of 5 spec-vs-substrate + producer-gate faces.\n\nF36.A2 (cross-flag interaction at feature emission): on root substrate, feature emission is non-additively gated. DEFAULT=16 features, --frameworks all=0, --include-docs=0, --frameworks all --include-docs=16. Each single flag suppresses features; combining restores them. Cross-flag interaction is not documented at run --help or spec §13.\n\nF36.B2 + F36.D5 (producer-gated features, substrate-level proof): --no-handler-slices zeros features (16→0) while preserving nodes/edges; features ARE handler-slice output, confirming pass-33 F33.18 at producer level. Independent substrate evidence: on root --include-docs substrate, all 16 default-features' entry_node IDs still exist as nodes (16/16 resolve in DOCS substrate) but features array is empty — feature producer is silently disabled by --include-docs even though substrate has needed inputs. Spec §13 framing 'named slices of the codebase' is wrong; features = handler-slice output only.\n\nF36.C1 (framework-linker activation universality): pass-34 F34.A1 33-violation breakdown (route-materializer 19 + grpc-linker 11 + graphql-linker 2) is per-codebase-specific. On tracker-pkg with --fw all, 20/20 violations are route-materializer ONLY; grpc-linker and graphql-linker absent (no .proto/.graphql files). Decomposition: route-materializer fires universally (grammar-independent); grpc/graphql fire grammar-files-present-conditionally.\n\nF36.C4 (codebase-specific feature suppression): F34.A2 + F35.A2 'features=0 on --fw all/--include-docs' is root-codebase-specific, NOT universal. Tracker substrate preserves features=16 across all 4 modes (default/fw_all/docs/combo). Pass-34/35 framing 'feature emission gated on auto-detect mode only' must narrow to '...on root codebase only.' Codebase-shape parameter affects which writer-passes fire.\n\nF36.B1 (compact subcommand EP truncation): --compact substrate has entrypoints=33 vs DEFAULT 104 (68% loss) while preserving features=16 + nodes/edges unchanged. Asymmetric truncation — compact silently drops 71 entrypoint records while preserving other top-level surfaces. Compact's truncation policy isn't documented at --help, parallels INV-pazur 'nodes_summary reports pre-shrink counts' family of compact-side gaps."  # 334d
