  clock: 16  # aeaa
  nonce: aeaa  # aeaa
  message: "Pass 37 (continuing 06022026_1700) batch of 5 cross-flag + compact-truncation faces.\n\nF37.C1 (cross-flag gate fragility — generalizes pass-36 F36.A2): single-flag feature-suppression (--fw all OR --docs each zeros features on root) is DEFEATED by adding ANY second flag except --no-handler-slices. Tested 7 combos pass-37 probe C: --compact + --docs (16) / --no-hs + --docs (0, --no-hs dominates) / --first-party-only + --docs (16) / --compact + --fw all (16) / --first-party-only + --fw all (16) / triple --fw all + --docs + --fp (16) / triple --fw all + --docs + --compact (16). 5 of 5 non-no-hs 2-flag combos restore features. Pattern consistent with buggy gate logic at the feature-emission write site, e.g., 'if exactly_one(--fw-all, --docs): suppress_features' or 'if len([f for f in [--fw-all, --docs] if f]) == 1: suppress'. F36.A2's 'non-additive restoration' framing should be reframed as 'gate fragility'.\n\nF37.B1 (compact EP-truncation algorithm): pass-36 F36.B1 showed --compact drops 71/104 EPs. Pass-37 characterizes: --compact keeps EP iff target node survives node selection (DEFAULT EPs whose symbol_id in COMPACT node set = 33/104; COMPACT EPs whose symbol_id in COMPACT node set = 33/33; KEPT set EXACTLY equals default EPs with symbol in compact node set). No independent EP-selection logic; EP array tracks node array.\n\nF37.B2+B3 (compact drop distribution — per-kind + per-package): heavy asymmetric preservation.\n- By kind: http_route 0% / html_entry 0% / script_module 0% / main_function 36.4% / shell_script 80.6% / library_export 82.6%.\n- By package: .githooks/* 0% / htrac-frontend 0% / hypergumbo-tracker/src 6.7% / hypergumbo-core/src 88.2% / lang-rust-analyzer/src 77.8% / scripts/ bash 100% / scripts/ python 0%.\nImplication: compact node-selection algorithm has implicit codebase-region bias. Web-facing surfaces (HTTP routes, HTML entries) and small one-off scripts preserved; core library code and bash utility scripts dropped.\n\nF37.B4 (missing truncation marker on entrypoints): compact substrate has NO 'entrypoints_truncated=True' field or 'original_count=104' field. Consumer must compare EP-count against unknown baseline to detect 71 missing records. Same shape as INV-pazur 'nodes_summary reports pre-shrink counts' extended to entrypoints array; sub-pattern (2) writer-conditioned-on-context applied to the truncation-marker layer. Fix candidate: add a top-level 'truncation' object with per-array original_count + flag.\n\nF37.C3 (writer-level vs EP-level effects orthogonal except on features): --no-handler-slices + --include-docs probe surfaces EPs=108 (DOCS adds 4 cli_command) with features=0 (--no-hs zeros features). Confirms --no-hs suppresses feature writer specifically; --include-docs adds EP records orthogonally. Both flags compose cleanly on EPs but features axis is non-orthogonal."  # aeaa
