  message: "Pass 38 (2026-06-02, dogfooding) — 2 findings batched:\n\nF38.A1: Feature writer SOLE = _emit_handler_slices at cli.py:7488. Selection criteria: _is_route_symbol(sym) AND not is_test_file(sym.path). _is_route_symbol (cli.py:7298) returns True when meta.framework_role=='route' OR meta.concepts[].concept=='route'. No flag-conditional suppression in the feature writer itself. Confirms pass-36 F36.B2 framing 'features = handler-slice output' is producer-level true; spec §13 'named slices' framing is wrong (sibling INV-luhur spec-drift face).\n\nF38.A2: Pass-37 F37.C1 'gate fragility' hypothesis (if exactly_one(--fw-all, --docs): suppress) is EMPIRICALLY REFUTED. Tracker --fw all has features=16 (same as default). Tracker --include-docs has features=16. Tracker default: 8 framework_role=route → 16 features. Tracker --fw all: 27 framework_role=route (19 in test paths filtered by is_test_file) + 141 concept=route → still 16 features after dedup + non-test filter. F36.C4 'tracker preserves features=16 across all 4 modes' framing supersedes F37.C1. Feature suppression on ROOT is codebase-specific, not gate-logic-specific. Actual mechanism likely involves root-only interaction between materialize_route_symbols + is_test_file path-prefix filter (deferred to pass-39+ with regenerated ROOT --fw all substrate). Pass-37 F37.C1 should be retitled 'root-codebase-specific feature suppression under flag-conditional materialization' (substrate evidence corrected)."  # 4fa1
