  message: "Pass 39 (2026-06-02, dogfooding) — 2 findings batched, INVALIDATING multi-pass false-claim chain:\n\nF39.A1 (HEADLINE — SUPERSEDES pass-34 F34.A2 + pass-35 F35.A2 + pass-36 F36.A2 + pass-37 F37.C1): ROOT --fw all features=16 (NOT 0). Fresh substrate regeneration (2× independent reproductions: 140873241 and 140873217 bytes, 34285 nodes, 109942 edges, 105 EPs, 33 validator violations EXACTLY matching pass-34 F34.A1) produces 16 features identical to ROOT default. Slice directory contains 8 handler slice files + 1 index — identical to ROOT default. The pass-34→35→36→37 chain claiming features=0/non-additive/gate-fragile on ROOT was built on a single mismeasurement that propagated across 4 passes. Pass-38 F38.A2 partially refuted F37.C1 via tracker; pass-39 fully refutes via root reproducibility.\n\nF39.A2: ROOT --include-docs features=16 (NOT 0). Fresh substrate produces 16 features + 4321 id_format violations (F35.A1 confirmed). Doc-analyzer id_format violations and feature emission are ORTHOGONAL — flag activates writers that violate id_format but does not suppress handler-slice features. Pass-35 F35.A2 / pass-36 F36.A2 likewise wrong.\n\nLesson: a substantive negative finding that repeats across passes should be verified by fresh substrate generation before pattern-amplifying. The pass-34→37 chain illustrates multi-pass amplification of single mismeasurement. Methodological scope note added.\n\nImplication for prior INV-luhur annotations: the 'FIRST validator-scope blind spot' framing from F34.A1+F34.A3 (33 violations on --fw all) is still CORRECT (re-confirmed in pass-39); the 'features=0 across 5 modes' from F34.A2 is WITHDRAWN. F35.A1 'SECOND validator-scope blind spot at 4321 violations on --include-docs' STILL CORRECT (re-confirmed). The 'cross-flag non-additivity' (F36.A2) and 'gate fragility' (F37.C1) framings are WITHDRAWN — there is no such gate behavior. F37.B1+B2+B3+B4 (--compact characterization) UNAFFECTED. F36.B1 (--compact EP truncation) UNAFFECTED. F36.D5 (substrate-level features=0 evidence on root DOCS) WITHDRAWN — pass-39 directly contradicts.\n\nSubstrate evidence: ROOT --fw all 8 framework_role=route non-test + 19 framework_role=route in-test-paths (filtered by is_test_file) + 141 concept=route + 19 materialized_from-bearing → 16 features after dedup + non-test filter. ROOT --include-docs 8 framework_role=route + 8 concept=route → 16 features. ROOT default 8 + 8 → 16 features (cached). All three reach the same feature set via different aggregate symbol counts.\n\nValidator-scope finding F34.A1 / F35.A1 / F35.A3 (profile.frameworks 3 distinct semantics across modes) STAND. The original CLAIM that WI-kafar CI gate operates against default substrate only and misses --fw-all/--include-docs writer paths remains true — the doc/config and framework-linker writers do escape exercise, producing 33+4321 violations on flagged modes. That's the live finding."  # a7ed
