- op: edit-msg-text  # 7c22
  at: '2026-06-04T17:40:26.594315Z'  # 7c22
  by: agent  # 7c22
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 7c22
  clock: 21  # 7c22
  nonce: 7c22  # 7c22
  item: INV-luhur-sital-lonar-tagiv-kuzab-mokol-jikot-fosug  # 7c22
  target_nonce: 78b8  # 7c22
  new_text: "**Pass-23 substrate-verified face (F23.2) — AnalysisRun.toolchain.name** (F23.3 disjoint language catalogs migrated to WI-ziror; F23.4 AR list ordering migrated to WI-haguz; F23.5 sub-schema versioning migrated to WI-romup per fold-audit Phase 2b).\n\n**(F23.2) `AnalysisRun.toolchain.name = \"python\"` for ALL 84 ARs, including grammar-based passes.** Distinct from WI-mipul (which is about ARs lacking the toolchain extension at all): this is about the value-semantic of `toolchain.name` even when populated. `rust` AR has `toolchain={'grammar_module': 'tree_sitter_rust', 'name': 'python', ...}`; `swift` AR has `grammar_module='tree_sitter_swift'` but `name='python'`. Field NAME suggests analyzer-language; VALUE is runtime. Same sub-pattern (3) \"same name, two definitions across paths\" as INV-pubom/INV-mozaf, but at the AR-toolchain layer. Either rename `toolchain.name → toolchain.runtime_name` + add `toolchain.analyzer_name`, or change the writer to record analyzer language.\n\nFace-level extension of INV-luhur. Will surface in WI-mipul's tail or future related WIs as appropriate.\n\n**Lab notebook entry:** `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_06022026_0010_pass23.md`."  # 7c22
  reason: "fold-audit 2b: F23.3/4/5 migrated; F23.2 kept"  # 7c22
- op: edit-msg-text  # 5643
  at: '2026-06-04T17:40:27.078942Z'  # 5643
  by: agent  # 5643
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 5643
  clock: 22  # 5643
  nonce: '5643'  # 5643
  item: INV-luhur-sital-lonar-tagiv-kuzab-mokol-jikot-fosug  # 5643
  target_nonce: a24a  # 5643
  new_text: "Pass-26 provenance-chain + producer-consumer probes — INV-luhur findings staying on this row (F26.1 metrics.languages.<lang>.nodes attribution migrated to WI-movah; F26.6 profile.loc double-count migrated to WI-palon per fold-audit Phase 2b).\n\nF26.15 (pass-25 F25.5 / F25.14 reframing — methodological): Both pass-25 findings overstated structural issues that are actually intentional, documented design.\n\n- F25.14 framed the JSON-field `pass` vs concept term `pass_id` as a naming-asymmetry trap. Per spec.md line 272 (\"pass_id: str # e.g., \\\"python\\\" (serialized as \\\"pass\\\" in JSON output).\") and line 717 (\"**Output-specific note:** The IR field `pass_id` is serialized as `pass` in JSON output.\"), the alias is documented intentional design. ir.py:275 emits `\"pass\": self.pass_id` deliberately. Pass-25's \"rename the field or concept\" recommendation was unnecessary — the alias is canonical. The probe-debug cost (calling `ar.get('pass_id')` returns None silently for 84/84 ARs) is real but is a probe-author concern, not a structural bug.\n\n- F25.5 framed AR.origin_run_id as \"100% NULL on all 84 ARs\" — but AR does not have an `origin_run_id` field at all. The dataclass (ir.py:194-217) only has `execution_id` (and `pass_id`, `version`, `run_signature`, `repo_fingerprint`, `toolchain`, `config_fingerprint`, files_*, skipped_*, failed_*, warnings, started_at, duration_ms, pass_version). spec.md line 1776 explicitly documents: \"nodes[].origin_run_id: String, references analysis_runs[].execution_id\" — the producer-side identity and consumer-side FK are named differently because they play different roles (database-style identity vs reference naming). The \"100% NULL\" measurement is actually \"field absent from record\"; pass-25 used `.get()` which silently returns None for missing keys, conflating the two.\n\nBoth reframings have a common root: Python's `.get('field', default=None)` returns None for both \"field present and explicitly None\" AND \"field absent from record\". Future cross-format probes should distinguish: `'field' in record` vs `record.get('field') is None`. Pass-25 used the wrong test in two places; pass-26 found this by grepping spec.md before drawing structural conclusions.\n\nImplications: INV-janob (the parent naming-asymmetry framing for F25.5) may need scope rewording — the asymmetry IS documented as design. The remaining INV-janob concern is whether a *consumer* migrating between bm.json versions needs translation help (a separate concern from \"is the asymmetry a bug\"). Pass-25's filing on INV-luhur for F25.14 stands as a probe-methodology observation but not a structural claim.\n\nF26.13 (positive confirmation of WI-mipul scope): pass_version='' cohort is EXACTLY WI-mipul's 14-target set — csharp, enclosure-linker, go, html, java, javascript, json, make, manifest_targets, play-routes, python, toml, xml, yaml_ansible. Set equality verified (∩=14, A\\B=∅, B\\A=∅). WI-mipul's scope holds without revision. Pass-26 adds: pass_version='' is the **empty-string sentinel** form (consistent with F25.4 origin_run_id='', F24.2 partial_results_reason=''). All three are reserved-empty-as-empty-string anti-patterns; the schema declares the field with str type and the producer writes '' rather than omitting."  # 5643
  reason: "fold-audit 2b: F26.1+F26.6 migrated; F26.15+F26.13 kept"  # 5643
- op: edit-msg-text  # ebe9
  at: '2026-06-04T17:40:27.562340Z'  # ebe9
