  item: INV-luhur-sital-lonar-tagiv-kuzab-mokol-jikot-fosug  # ebe9
  target_nonce: ca99  # ebe9
  new_text: "Pass-30 spec.md drift findings — INV-luhur faces staying on this row (F30.5 evidence_type vocab drift → WI-guvup; F30.6 edge.type vocab drift → WI-dinih; F30.7 feature record shape drift → WI-zikot; F30.10 scs.derived_skipped schema deviation → WI-gabos; F30.13 io-boundaries CLI recomputes → WI-puvun; F30.14 Node.meta 42 undocumented sub-keys → WI-mirig per fold-audit Phase 2b).\n\nPass 30 ran two-way schema audit walking spec.md §6 + §9 against the substrate at /tmp/hg-dogfood-s21/bm.json. Sub-pattern (4) \"two-analyzer-cohorts-two-surfaces\" applied to spec-narrative-vs-substrate at scale.\n\n**F30.1 — Top-level scheme-identifier drift (probe 1.A).**\n- spec §9.667 example shows schema_version='0.2.1'; substrate has '0.13.0' (4 major versions out of date in spec narrative). Beyond WI-foful's stableid v2→v5 + canonical_name removal scope.\n- spec §6.373 documents stable_id_scheme='hypergumbo-stableid-v2'; substrate has 'hypergumbo-stableid-v5'. (Known.)\n- bm.symbol_fingerprint_scheme='hypergumbo-symbol-fp-v1' is present in substrate but NOT documented in spec §6.373-375 (which lists only 3 schemes). 4th scheme exists with its own writer at top-level.\n\n**F30.2 — Bonus reframing of pass-27 F27.6**: F27.6 said \"bm.fingerprint_scheme=None top-level reserved-empty\"; substrate ACTUALLY has the key absent entirely (not None-valued), AND spec doesn't declare a bare `fingerprint_scheme` field. F27.6 was a probe error (.get() returning None for absent key, same finding-family as F28.1 / F26.15 / F27.5). Real state: 4 prefixed scheme fields, all populated; no `fingerprint_scheme` (bare) exists or is reserved.\n\n**F30.3 — Top-level keys (probe 1.B).** 22 actual top-level keys vs 19 documented in §9 example block. 3 undocumented: supply_chain_summary, symbol_fingerprint_scheme (above), validation_report. validation_report is INV-sugat's artifact; supply_chain_summary is ADR-0024 territory. Neither appears in the §9.664-682 top-level structure example.\n\n**F30.8 — Edge.meta documented-but-100%-absent (probe 1.H).** Spec §9.811-822 documents 15 meta sub-fields; substrate has 22 distinct. 100% absent from substrate: receiver, evidence[] (multi-pass), io_boundary, io_primitive, taint_labels, taint_sanitized_by. Of these:\n- taint_labels / taint_sanitized_by are conditional-design (only when verify-claims runs taint propagation) — design-correct.\n- evidence[], receiver documented as available; substrate 0%.\n- io_boundary / io_primitive (ADR-0016) spec §9.818 says \"Stamped on every call edge whose target is...a primitive.\" Substrate-side stamping is 0% (io-boundaries CLI recomputes — now under WI-puvun).\n\nSame finding-family as pass-28 F28.3 (evidence_lang / evidence_spans 0% absent via conditional-write suppression).\n\n**Coverage tally.** Of 14 substantive spec-narrative claims about substrate structure that pass 30 measured against substrate, 4 MATCH cleanly (shape_id_scheme, repo_fingerprint_scheme, confidence_model, view) + 1 §9.781 presence-rule HOLDS exactly (stable_id/shape_id key always present). 9 of 14 DRIFT (substantive divergence between spec narrative and substrate observation). DRIFT rate: 64% (9/14) of spec-narrative claims measured.\n\nSpec.md §9 is currently a substantially-stale snapshot of the substrate shape. The dataclass layer is more current (CI-enforced via `scripts/generate-schema --check`), but the narrative isn't gated; pass-29 F29.1 showed dataclass-narrative drift; pass-30 shows the substrate-narrative drift is wider. Fix-path candidate (human-decision): a generated §9 from `docs/schema.json`, OR a CI check that walks §9 string-literal claims against schema.json.\n\nNo status change. Pass-30 supplies the structural inventory for INV-luhur's spec-drift face at scale across §6 and §9.\n\nProbe artifacts: /tmp/pass30_probe1.py (20 sub-probes) + /tmp/pass30_probe2.py + /tmp/pass30_probe2b.py + /tmp/pass30_probe2c.py. Outputs in /tmp/pass30_output*.log."  # ebe9
  reason: "fold-audit 2b: F30.5/6/7/10/13/14 migrated; F30.1/2/3/8 kept"  # ebe9
- op: edit-msg-text  # cd79
  at: '2026-06-04T17:40:28.054583Z'  # cd79
  by: agent  # cd79
  actor: jgstern_agent  # cd79
  clock: 24  # cd79
  nonce: cd79  # cd79
  item: INV-luhur-sital-lonar-tagiv-kuzab-mokol-jikot-fosug  # cd79
  target_nonce: 8f71  # cd79
  new_text: "Pass-31 spec-drift batch — INV-luhur faces staying on this row (F31.2 production-functions derivation migrated to WI-rakol per fold-audit Phase 2b; F31.3 verify-claims schema, F31.6 sketch --input perf, F31.7 subcommand perf profile retained).\n\n**F31.3 — verify-claims YAML schema entirely undocumented in spec.md narrative.** Accepted YAML fields (from packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/verify_claims.py:188-228 load_claims()):\n```yaml\nschema_version: 1\nclaims:\n  - id: <str>\n    text: <str>\n    constraint:\n      boundary: <str>  # I/O boundary name\n      must_not_exist: <bool>\n      max_chains: <int>\n      taint_flow:\n        source_taint: <str>\n        prohibited_sink_zone: <str>\n        allowed_sanitizers: <list[str]>\n```\nSpec.md §6 (Internal representation), §9 (Behavior map JSON), §10 (Sketch output), §11 (Slicing behavior) don't describe this schema. ADR-0017 (taint propagation) hints at the taint_flow sub-fields but the constraint envelope is not spec'd. Consumers writing claim YAMLs have no spec-level reference; they must read load_claims() in verify_claims.py. INV-luhur spec-narrative face.\n\nFix-path candidate: a dedicated §10b or §12 in spec.md formalizing the claims schema; OR an authoritative `docs/claims-schema.md` with JSON Schema.\n\n**F31.6 — sketch --input cannot complete on cached substrate within 5 minutes; --help claim \"Use cached results file instead of re-analyzing (faster)\" is materially incorrect for substrate at this codebase scale.**\n\n```\nsketch --input bm.json -t 8000 --no-secret-scan --no-progress  → timeout at 5m (exit 124)\nsketch --input bm.json -t 2000 --no-secret-scan --no-progress  → timeout at 3m (exit 124)\nsketch /home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo/packages/hypergumbo-tracker -t 4000 --no-secret-scan  → completes in <90s, produces 415-line Markdown\n```\n\nThe --input path is materially slower than the fresh-analysis path (which DOES complete). For a 140MB substrate / 34253-node graph, sketch --input apparently does O(repo-size × something) redundant work that the fresh path bypasses. INV-papuj already umbrellas \"sketch read-path does redundant computation when authoritative data is on disk\"; pass-31 supplies the substrate-level quantification: not just \"slower,\" but \"doesn't complete within 5 minutes at any token budget tested.\"\n\nThe --help claim \"faster\" is the INV-rotup-family drift: --help text doesn't match behavior at codebase scale.\n\nFix-path candidate: profile sketch --input on this substrate; the perf gap suggests an O(N²) or O(N × M) loop that's avoided in the fresh path; OR fix the --help text to reflect the perf reality.\n\n**F31.7 — substrate subcommand performance profile.**\n\n| Tier | Subcommand | --input wall-clock |\n|---|---|---|\n| Fast (<3s) | cache-status | 0.28s |\n| | routes | 1.17s |\n| | search | 1.19s |\n| | test-coverage | 2.23s |\n| | verify-claims (valid YAML) | 2.47s |\n| | explain Symbol | 2.85s |\n| | io-boundaries | 2.86s |\n| | symbols (--limit 200 default) | 2.92s |\n| Medium (3-15s) | compact | 5.00s |\n| | symbols --all | 12.57s |\n| Slow (60s+) | dead-code-maybe | ~90s |\n| Won't-complete (>5m) | sketch (--input, any token budget) | timeout exit 124 |\n\n`symbols --all` scales 4.3× the default (12.57s vs 2.92s) — proportional and expected. Slow-cluster (dead-code-maybe, sketch) is 1-2 orders of magnitude slower than fast-cluster. Documentation should set this expectation; users currently have no signal about per-subcommand wall-clock characteristics. Maps to existing umbrellas WI-tuduf (bash analyzer 15x slower per-file) for per-pass analysis and INV-papuj for sketch redundant computation.\n\nNo status change. Pass-31 supplies 3 spec-drift faces — verify-claims schema documentation gap, sketch --input perf claim contradiction, and the broader subcommand performance profile.\n\nProbe artifacts: /tmp/pass31_probeA.py + outputs; sketch tests in /tmp/p31_sketch*.md."  # cd79
  reason: "fold-audit 2b: F31.2 migrated; F31.3/6/7 kept"  # cd79
- op: edit-msg-text  # ef2a
  at: '2026-06-04T17:42:56.272336Z'  # ef2a
  by: agent  # ef2a
  actor: jgstern_agent  # ef2a
