  item: INV-luhur-sital-lonar-tagiv-kuzab-mokol-jikot-fosug  # ef2a
  target_nonce: '24e4'  # ef2a
  new_text: "Pass-32 spec-narrative & meta-layer drift batch — INV-luhur faces staying on this row (F32.2 files_analyzed non-determinism migrated to WI-bijad; F32.4 catalog pass-set vs substrate divergence migrated to WI-didil per fold-audit Phase 2b).\n\nPass-32 exercised pass-31's queued probe class \"hypergumbo catalog/config vs spec analyzer & linker lists.\" Remaining findings:\n\n**F32.3 — Three documentation surfaces give three linker counts.** spec.md §7 line 405 says \"the full catalog of 45 linkers grouped by subcategory\"; LINKERS.md's catalogue table has 46 entries and its bottom-line text says \"Count: 46 linkers — Protocol 13, Bridge 10, Framework 17, Infrastructure 6\"; `hypergumbo catalog` reports 58 linker-named passes (54 if the 5 view_template subfamilies fold to 1 logical linker). Three sources, three counts. After name-normalization (catalog hyphens → underscores, `_linker` suffix strip): 45 normalized linker names overlap with LINKERS.md's 46; LINKERS.md is missing one face (`subprocess_cli` is `subprocess-linker` in catalog) and catalog has 13 entries not in LINKERS.md (see F32.5). Drift is real: spec.md cites the smallest number, catalog has the largest, LINKERS.md sits in between but is also stale.\n\n**F32.5 — 8 linker passes shipped in catalog are absent from LINKERS.md.** After folding view_template subfamilies and normalizing names, LINKERS.md is missing 8 production linkers:\n```\n{controller_routes, router_routes, kafka_streams_dispatch, jackson_dispatch,\n django_orm_dispatch, airflow_framework_dispatch, rust_trait_dispatch,\n inherited_calls}\n```\nLINKERS.md's authoritative \"Count: 46\" line is wrong by at least 8 — actual production set is 54+ (after view_template fold). The cosmetic discrepancy of `subprocess` vs `subprocess_cli` is a minor rename face. Each missing linker is a distinct dispatch / framework / language-pair concern; their absence from LINKERS.md likely means downstream readers (consumers learning what linkers do) miss the corresponding fix-points.\n\n**F32.11 — `compact --help` documents \"summary of omitted symbols\" but the actual top-level output key is `nodes_summary`.** `hypergumbo compact --input … --out …` produces a top-level field `nodes_summary` (introducing 1 new key vs the input bm.json's 22 keys). `compact --help` text reads:\n```\nConverts an existing behavior map to compact form with:\n- Top symbols by centrality coverage (connectivity-aware selection by default)\n- Summary of omitted symbols (bag-of-words, path patterns, kinds)\n- Induced subgraph edges (only edges between included symbols)\n```\n\"Summary of omitted symbols\" implies a field named `summary` or `omitted_summary`. The actual field is `nodes_summary` — and per existing INV-pazur, its `included.count` overstates the actual `len(nodes)` in tiered emission. Two faces on the same field: name doesn't match documentation (F32.11), and the value doesn't match the data (INV-pazur). Sub-pattern (1) same-fact-two-names at help-text vs output-key.\n\n**F32.12 — `compact`'s \"selective truncation per top-level field\" rule is undocumented.** `hypergumbo compact` on the substrate produces a structurally near-identical bm.json (22 of 22 input top-level keys, +1 new `nodes_summary`). Of the 6 array-typed top-level fields:\n- nodes: 34253 → 100 (0.29%)        truncated\n- edges: 109915 → 370 (0.34%)       truncated\n- entrypoints: 104 → 33 (31.73%)    truncated (induced filter on symbol_id)\n- features: 16 → 16 (100%)          PRESERVED\n- usage_contexts: 8 → 8 (100%)      PRESERVED\n- analysis_runs: 84 → 84 (100%)     PRESERVED\nThe \"compact form\" promise applies asymmetrically — provenance metadata (analysis_runs, features) is not compacted, only the node/edge/entrypoint graph. This is plausibly correct design (provenance must survive to interpret the compact subgraph), but `--help` says \"Top symbols by centrality coverage\" without specifying which top-level fields are truncated vs preserved. Consumers of the compact output don't know without reading `compact.py:format_tiered_behavior_map` source. INV-luhur spec-narrative drift at the compact-format layer.\n\n**Probe artifacts.** /tmp/p32_probeA.py + p32_probeA2.py (run-vs-frozen diff producing F32.2 + F32.4-related counts); /tmp/p32_probeB.py (catalog vs substrate vs LINKERS.md, producing F32.3-5); /tmp/p32_probeD.py (compact behavior, producing F32.11-12)."  # ef2a
  reason: "fold-audit 2b: F32.2+F32.4 migrated; F32.3/5/11/12 kept"  # ef2a
