  new_text: "Pass-35 batch — INV-luhur face staying on this row (F35.A1 second validator-scope blind spot at 4321 --include-docs violations migrated to WI-himoj (consolidates with F34.A1) per fold-audit Phase 2b; F35.A3 profile.frameworks 3-mode semantics retained).\n\n**F35.A3 — profile.frameworks has 3 distinct semantics across flag modes.** Sweep across 6 modes:\n- DEFAULT, FIRST_PARTY, INCLUDE_DOCS, MAX_TIER_4: ['lit', 'starlette'] (detection-derived per substrate content)\n- FW_ALL: 171 entries (full catalog dump, per pass-34 F34.A3)\n- FW_NONE: [] (silenced entirely)\n\nSame field — 3 distinct behaviors. Pass-34 F34.A3 documented the catalog-dump face; pass-35 confirms detection is consistent across 4 other modes AND adds the `--fw none` silenced-entirely face. Cross-mode survey establishes that the field carries 3 semantic categories with no in-record signal to distinguish them — consumers reading profile.frameworks cannot tell which mode produced the value without out-of-band knowledge.\n\nFix-path candidates for F35.A3: split into `frameworks_requested` vs `frameworks_detected`; deprecate the flag-echo behavior and always emit detected; document the 3-mode semantics. (Validator-scope and id_format fix paths now under WI-himoj and INV-kurup respectively.)\n\n**Probe artifacts:** `/tmp/p35_docs.json` (142 MB substrate); `/tmp/p35_probeA.py` validator-scope sweep script; `/tmp/p35_outputA.log` (violation breakdown across 6 modes)."  # f269
