  new_text: "Pass 36 (continuing 06022026_1622) batch — INV-luhur faces staying on this row (F36.B1 compact EP truncation migrated to WI-kulan per fold-audit Phase 2b; F36.A2 / F36.C4 / F36.D5 INVALIDATED by pass-39 F39.A1 but preserved as methodology-calibration record).\n\nF36.A2 (cross-flag interaction at feature emission — INVALIDATED by F39.A1): original framing claimed on root substrate, feature emission is non-additively gated. DEFAULT=16 features, --frameworks all=0, --include-docs=0, --frameworks all --include-docs=16. Each single flag suppresses features; combining restores them. Pass-39 fresh-substrate verification refuted this — ROOT --fw all features=16 (not 0). Multi-pass mismeasurement-amplification record.\n\nF36.B2 + F36.D5 (producer-gated features, substrate-level proof): --no-handler-slices zeros features (16→0) while preserving nodes/edges; features ARE handler-slice output, confirming pass-33 F33.18 at producer level (now under WI-tovap). F36.D5's \"all 16 default-features' entry_node IDs still exist as nodes (16/16 resolve in DOCS substrate) but features array is empty\" was also INVALIDATED by F39.A2 — ROOT --include-docs features=16.\n\nF36.C1 (framework-linker activation universality): pass-34 F34.A1 33-violation breakdown (route-materializer 19 + grpc-linker 11 + graphql-linker 2) is per-codebase-specific. On tracker-pkg with --fw all, 20/20 violations are route-materializer ONLY; grpc-linker and graphql-linker absent (no .proto/.graphql files). Decomposition: route-materializer fires universally (grammar-independent); grpc/graphql fire grammar-files-present-conditionally. (INV-bikaj scope extension.)\n\nF36.C4 (codebase-specific feature suppression — INVALIDATED): original framing claimed F34.A2 + F35.A2 'features=0 on --fw all/--include-docs' is root-codebase-specific, NOT universal. Pass-38 F38.A2 and pass-39 F39.A1 invalidated the entire 4-pass chain; preserved here as methodology record."  # 362d
